@page "/"

<PageTitle>Blazor learning sandbox</PageTitle>
<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Large" Class="pa-4 pb-8">
    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-4" Outlined>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.overline" Color="Color.Primary">Learn by changing working examples</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h3" HtmlTag="h1">Your Blazor and MudBlazor toolbox</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="p" Class="my-4">Explore focused labs, inspect the source, and experiment with the tradeoffs.</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">Start with component state. Progress through forms, data grids, APIs, SQLite, authentication, localization, files, and observability. Each lab includes an exercise and explains the lifetime of its data.</MudText>
        <MudStack Row Class="flex-wrap">
            <MudButton Href="/counter" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary">Start learning</MudButton>
            <MudButton Href="/labs" Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary">Explore all labs</MudButton>
            <MudButton Href="https://github.com/jonathanperis/blazor-mudblazor-starter" Target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source</MudButton>
        </MudStack>
    </MudPaper>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mb-3">A small app with room to experiment</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-4">.NET 10, MudBlazor 9, synthetic datasets, and a local SQLite notebook. Cloud accounts are optional. The default labs are designed for learning, with explicit boundaries between demonstration code and deployment concerns.</MudText>
    <MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-4" Outlined>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">Run locally</MudText>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/jonathanperis/blazor-mudblazor-starter.git
cd blazor-mudblazor-starter
dotnet run --project src/WebClient</code></pre>
        <MudLink Href="https://jonathanperis.github.io/blazor-mudblazor-starter/docs/getting-started/">Setup and learning guide</MudLink>
    </MudPaper>
    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Variant="Variant.Outlined">Counter and grid experiments reset with their component or circuit. The SQLite notebook survives restarts on the same data volume and is scoped to your browser workspace.</MudAlert>
</MudContainer>
